Z||000000||Richard Parnell||06-11-2001||02:18 PM||||Does anyone know what type of relay the one for the ac is.  It's the one in the engine compartment on the left side of the fire wall.  There are two relays there.  I don't know what the outer one is for but the inner one is for the AC and is inop.  Also is it avalable at NAPA?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Richard Parnell||06-11-2001||03:32 PM||||Anyone?||||reg||5
Z||000002||87GTZ34||06-11-2001||04:05 PM||||Yes you should be able to get it at NAPA.  It is not unique to the Fiero.  The outer one should be the fuel pump relay and they are interchangeable.  GL||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||06-11-2001||06:39 PM||||I agree that the relays are generally interchange-able, check the numbers on the side.  The manual says the other relay is the high speed blower relay.  I would remove the relay and go to local GM dealer and they can get you one from the numbers off the side||||reg||1
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||06-11-2001||07:14 PM||||Thanks||||reg||6
Z||000005||87GTZ34||06-12-2001||01:15 AM||||Opps.  Sorry, i was assuming it was a six like mine where the fp and ac relays are side by side behind the driver.  I just looked up the relays in my '87 book...  It shows 3 relays side by side behind the driver: leftmost coolant fan; center AC; rightmost fuelpump relay. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
